  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve SP&amp;LR for WFs in ASEAN Agri-food</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2026, 5000 women farmers and agricultural workers and indigenous women be strengthened to support social protection and their rights for gender equality, resilience and for agroecology.

Objective 1:  To contribute with evidence-based knowledge and documentation regarding the risks and vulnerabilities that women farmers and agricultural workers face, including insights into vulnerabilitiescaused by climate change, which will provide the basis for advocacy work.

Result 1: Relevant ASEAN structures put the respect of gender transformative and shock responsive SP and labour rights of women workers in the agri-food sector on the political agenda of the member states.
Documentation regarding risks and vulnerabilities of women farmers and workers caused by climate change and impactof COVID-19 in the food and agricultural production contribute to the overall advocacy to support.

Objective 2: To support cross-sectoral alliance building between the rural women farmers movements and labour right movements, introducing the labour rights and social protection issues in the work of the network members.

Result 2: Regional networks align and cooperate around a common ambitionto promote the rights of women workers in the agri-food sector to decent workand shock &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; gender-responsive social protection.</narrative>
  </description>
